ation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"f957a819-1d81-4eb9-912f-56173ffb8d6d","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"ae28-cf13-f465-400b"}],"description":"## Context\n\nBefore any change-size/decomposition rule can enter the DET floor, measure whether change shape actually drives the defect-rework loop here (11-plan-v3 I-4; measurement-first matches the field — Prow's `size/*` labels are non-blocking, 12c). Tooling anchor (12a): extend `scripts/backtest_bugfix_size.py` (442 lines), which imports the shipped predicate `BUGFIX_SIZE_THRESHOLD_NON_TEST_LINES` and `escalation_for_diff` from `rebar.llm.code_review.bugfix_size_gate` so its threshold cannot drift from the gate that ships. 2026 grounding (12b): MSR'26 agentic-PR studies show files-touched/commit fragmentation is a sharper variable than raw LOC, the size-quality relationship is nonstationary (re-tune, never freeze), and context fragmentation is an independent causal variable (39% quality drop in a controlled study). The two doubling friction categories (CI-at-landing 25/60; environment 13/60 — R2S3) are unexplained and get mechanism reads, not guesses.\n\n## Approach\n\n**Step 0 — overlap check, before building.** 11-plan-v3 I-4 requires confirming this does not duplicate the Tier-2 replay harness (ADR 0109, `1299d9deb6da`, `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/`). The finding is recorded in the backtest report's Method section either way; if the harness already supplies a variable, this task consumes it rather than re-deriving it.\n\n**Read (a) — change shape.** Extend the backtest with an all-work mode (not just bug-typed tickets) measuring rework against three variables: non-test LOC (via the already-imported `count_non_test_diff_lines`), files touched (`git show --name-only`), and commit fragmentation (commits per ticket, grouped by the `rebar-ticket:` trailer). The script computes no correlation today — only a recall summary — so this adds a statistical layer rather than extending one. **Rework signals — two, both PER-TICKET and both offline.** (i) store `caused_by` fan-in, the same label source the script already uses, and (ii) gate rounds: how many `REVIEW_RESULT` / `COMPLETION_VERDICT` events a ticket accumulated. Both are read per ticket id, so both join on the key above. The `rebar metrics` proxies are NOT usable here and are deliberately excluded: `revert_recovery` and `reopen_recovery` return a single REPO-WIDE int and `first_pass_rate` a single REPO-WIDE float, so they have no per-ticket value to correlate against; only `attempts_per_ticket` is per-ticket, and gate rounds subsume it. Gerrit patchset count is likewise excluded: it alone needs the network, making the corpus unreproducible offline.\n\n**The join key, explicitly.** Shape is measured PER COMMIT; rework is measured PER TICKET, so the two are aligned on the **full canonical rebar ticket id** taken from each commit's FIRST `rebar-ticket:` trailer (parsed with the shipped `extract_ticket_refs`). `group_by_ticket` SUMS per-commit shape into per-ticket aggregates (non-test LOC, total LOC, commit count) and unions files-touched; that row is what correlates. A commit whose trailer does not resolve to exactly one full canonical id in the store — an ambiguous 4-quad fragment, or a ticket no longer present — is UNJOINABLE: it is excluded from the correlation and its count is reported, never silently dropped. This is also why the window starts 2026-07-01: trailer coverage on `origin/main` is 60/650 in June (pre-enforcement, unjoinable) against 876/907 in July.\n\n**Read (b) — CI-at-landing.** The doubling window is 2026-08-25..2026-08-30 (the newer-30 half of R2S3's 60 session logs). No case list is committed, so the 20 cases are derived: session-log mining over that window for `Verified -1` / CI-failure patterns, cross-referenced to the specific Gerrit changes R2S3 already names. Each case is read for mechanism, change shape, cross-session interference, isolation class, and drift class.\n\n**Read (c) — environment.** Session reports are `session_log` tickets, queryable offline via `rebar session-logs -o json`. The automated `llm-degrade NEEDS_INVESTIGATION` logs carry a structured JSON body (`exception_type`, `message`, `model`) and are countable without keyword heuristics; the remainder are read for mechanism. Output projects specific fields — a full dump is dominated by authorship ledgers and is unusably large.\n\n**Decision.** The size/decomposition enforcement decision is recorded either way as ADR 0110 (next free number; `docs/adr/.numbers/0110` marker committed alongside, which is the race-free uniqueness mechanism). `docs/adr/README.md` is GENERATED by `scripts/gen_adr_index.py` and must be regenerated, never hand-edited.\n\n**Dependency.** `reports/` is gitignored; the `.gitignore` re-inclusion of `reports/stability/` lands in sibling `yogic-soapstone-takin` (f9b9-83ad-931c-4833), which sits below this change in the stack. This task inherits it and adds no second `.gitignore` edit.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [x] AC1: `reports/stability/change-shape-backtest.md` is committed, giving the distribution of all three variables (non-test LOC, files touched, commit fragmentation) and each one's measured relationship to rework, with n stated inline. Verified by `git ls-files reports/stability/change-shape-backtest.md`.\n- [x] AC2: read (a) is reproducible — the report's Method section names the exact command, and re-running it reproduces the reported n. Verified by running the documented `python scripts/backtest_bugfix_size.py ...` invocation.\n- [x] AC3: `reports/stability/ci-landing-regressions-read.md` is committed with a 20-row per-case table (mechanism, change shape, class) and states how the cases were selected from the 2026-08-25..2026-08-30 window.\n- [x] AC4: `reports/stability/environment-failures-read.md` is committed with per-case mechanisms and a class disposition per case, naming which dispositions feed the doctor-checks scope.\n- [x] AC5: the enforcement decision is recorded either way as `docs/adr/0110-*.md` with its supporting evidence, and `docs/adr/.numbers/0110` is committed. Verified by `python scripts/gen_adr_index.py --check` exiting 0 and `python scripts/check_adr_numbers.py` confirming the bijection.\n- [x] AC6: the Step-0 overlap finding against ADR 0109's replay harness is stated in the backtest report, so a later reader knows the boundary was checked.\n- [x] AC7: the extended script still imports the shipped threshold predicate rather than re-deriving it, so the backtest cannot drift from the gate. Verified by the existing import remaining, exercised by the script's tests.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `python scripts/backtest_bugfix_size.py --check-planning-corpus` — the existing pinned-corpus self-check still passes, proving the all-work extension did not perturb the shipped bug-corpus path (AC7).\n- the documented all-work invocation from the report's Method section — re-runs read (a) and reproduces its n (AC2).\n- `python scripts/gen_adr_index.py --check` and `python scripts/check_adr_numbers.py` — the ADR is indexed and its number is uniquely claimed (AC5).\n- `git ls-files reports/stability/` — the three reports are tracked (AC1, AC3, AC4).\n- `make lint && make typecheck` — the script extension clears the house gates, including the complexity ratchet.\n\nMeasurement reads are evidence documents, not executable behavior, so their oracle is reproducibility (AC2) rather than a new automated test; the script change itself is covered by the pinned-corpus check above.\n\n## File impact\n\n- `scripts/backtest_bugfix_size.py` (extend: all-work mode + files-touched/fragmentation variables and the correlation layer)\n- `reports/stability/change-shape-backtest.md` (new)\n- `reports/stability/ci-landing-regressions-read.md` (new)\n- `reports/stability/environment-failures-read.md` (new)\n- `docs/adr/0110-<slug>.md` and `docs/adr/.numbers/0110` (new; the enforcement decision)\n- `docs/adr/README.md` (regenerated by `scripts/gen_adr_index.py`)","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"scripts/backtest_bugfix_size.py","reason":"all-work mode entrypoint + CLI"},{"path":"scripts/_backtest/__init__.py","reason":"extracted package: check_import_walk imports every top-level scripts/*.py standalone, so the mode's logic must live in a subpackage"},{"path":"scripts/_backtest/all_work.py","reason":"corpus walk, ticket grouping, rework signals, correlations, threshold split"},{"path":"scripts/_backtest/stats.py","reason":"quantiles, describe, rank transform, Spearman"},{"path":"reports/stability/change-shape-backtest.md","reason":"read (a) deliverable"},{"path":"reports/stability/change-shape-backtest.json","reason":"the --out artifact the report's reproduction command writes"},{"path":"reports/stability/ci-landing-regressions-read.md","reason":"read (b) deliverable"},{"path":"reports/stability/environment-failures-read.md","reason":"read (c) deliverable"},{"path":"docs/adr/0110-change-shape-advisory-not-blocking.md","reason":"the enforcement decision recorded either way"},{"path":"docs/adr/.numbers/0110","reason":"race-free ADR number claim"},{"path":"docs/adr/README.md","reason":"regenerated by gen_adr_index.py"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","87cb-7121-a3b6-4606"],["relates_to","ae28-cf13-f465-400b"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"87cb-7121-a3b6-4606","parent_status_uuid":"9124da14-f196-406e-87b9-0e99c476f9a9","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":["rebar"],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"0880-0afb-7fe3-48c9","ticket_type":"task","title":"Upstream introduction measurement: change-shape backtest + CI-at-landing and environment mechanism reads","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["6ee51304-708c-4489-8075-5d015c4aff47","23e5d09c-f41f-48e4-9787-a21e9c5eb0a3","f92498bb-0afc-4cab-bc1c-e025a878f395","9124da14-f196-406e-87b9-0e99c476f9a9","67c2f70a-414b-4161-b6d4-4b4da62ed0b9","f957a819-1d81-4eb9-912f-56173ffb8d6d","505b80d8-16b9-4ea3-afdf-0d1df16f0ad6","7a6ed438-9292-42be-94b5-414649acda0c","f5127f9f-5c7b-4ebe-bafe-77a971b91bf6","8371019c-5a44-4ee3-ad12-f1effddbf582","b28f07bd-7972-45e9-9dae-2ef96fe62ed2","6d5ed8a1-7594-44a4-8059-4fdc6b245318"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788351554148271431,"uuid":"dfa3f7d4-36f7-4b0a-95fc-9333a2bef3ee"}